# §268 — BUILD CONTEXT HYGIENE.
#
# §266 found this file absent while the Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, which means the ENTIRE backend
# working directory — including untracked local files — was uploaded into the build context and
# copied into the build stage. `backend/.env` lives there during normal development and carries
# DATABASE_URL, JWT_SECRET and ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. A build run from a developer machine therefore
# baked real credentials into an image layer.
#
# It matters even though the RUNTIME stage copies only `dist`, `scripts` and four `src/safescope-v2`
# data directories: the BUILD stage layer still contains whatever was copied, layers are part of the
# image's history, and anyone who can pull the image can read them.
#
# THE ORDERING BELOW IS DELIBERATE: broad excludes first, then re-includes for the few excluded
# paths the build genuinely needs. `scripts/release/*.js` is re-included because the runtime image
# runs the release migration from it.

# ---- secrets and local configuration. The reason this file exists.
# No re-include for .env.example: the build does not need it, and an absolute rule is one fewer
# thing to get wrong than a rule with a hole in it.
#
# NOTE THE `**/` PREFIXES. Docker anchors every pattern at the CONTEXT ROOT, so a bare `*.pem`
# excludes `private.pem` and does NOT exclude `tls/private.pem`. The §268 build-context guard
# caught exactly that hole in the first draft of this file, which is why each secret pattern is
# written twice — once anchored, once with `**/` — rather than trusting the bare form.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.key
**/*.key
*.p12
**/*.p12
*.pfx
**/*.pfx
*.keystore
**/*.keystore
id_rsa*
**/id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
**/id_ed25519*
*credentials*.json
**/*credentials*.json
*service-account*.json
**/*service-account*.json
.npmrc
**/.npmrc
.netrc
**/.netrc
secrets
**/secrets

# ---- dependencies and build output. Reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules
dist
build
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- verification evidence. Large, and the runtime needs none of it.

verification
evidence
*.sha256

# ---- local artifacts, caches and temporary files.
tmp
temp
tmp-*
*.log
*.tmp
.cache
.turbo
.parcel-cache
.eslintcache
uploads
storage-local

# ---- version control, CI and editor/system noise.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- test and documentation surfaces the runtime image does not execute.
test
__tests__
*.spec.ts
*.test.ts
docs

# ---- RE-INCLUDES. Everything below is needed by the build or the runtime.
# `scripts/` as a whole is NOT excluded above; these entries exist so that a future broad
# `scripts` exclusion cannot silently remove the release migration path from the image.
!scripts/release/migrate.js
!scripts/release/verify-running-sha.js
!scripts/render-start-diagnostic.js
